.IX Title "YaraFFI::Record::YR_META 3pm"
.TH YaraFFI::Record::YR_META 3pm 2025-10-30 "perl v5.38.2" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
YaraFFI::Record::YR_META \- FFI Record for YARA metadata structure
.SH VERSION
.IX Header "VERSION"
Version 0.07
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    use YaraFFI::Record::YR_META;
\&    use FFI::Platypus;
\&
\&    my $ffi = FFI::Platypus\->new(api => 2);
\&
\&    # In a YARA callback, cast metadata pointer to record
\&    my $meta = $ffi\->cast(\*(Aqopaque\*(Aq, \*(Aqrecord(YaraFFI::Record::YR_META)*\*(Aq, $meta_ptr);
\&
\&    # Access fields safely
\&    my $type = $meta\->type;
\&    my $id_ptr = $meta\->identifier;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Represents the YR_META structure from YARA's libyara. This allows safe
access to rule metadata through FFI::Platypus records.
.SH "STRUCTURE FIELDS"
.IX Header "STRUCTURE FIELDS"
.IP "type (sint32)" 4
.IX Item "type (sint32)"
Metadata type: 1=INTEGER, 2=STRING, 3=BOOLEAN
.IP "identifier (opaque)" 4
.IX Item "identifier (opaque)"
Pointer to the metadata identifier string
.IP "string (opaque)" 4
.IX Item "string (opaque)"
Pointer to string value (when type is STRING)
.IP "integer (sint64)" 4
.IX Item "integer (sint64)"
Integer value (when type is INTEGER)
